Reason: pin the revision of the sentence encoder SEMMA loads. flags.yaml selects jinaai, which transformers loads with trust_remote_code=True -- it downloads and executes custom_st.py from the model repository. Upstream passes no revision, so both that code and the weights are whatever main points at when the run happens. The container pins JINA_REVISION and caches that commit at build time, and runs set HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1, so the copy executed is the one the image was built against. Does not change which model is used, only which version of it.

diff --git a/ultra/tasks.py b/ultra/tasks.py
index 1894ff5..7c2b5e9 100644
--- a/ultra/tasks.py
+++ b/ultra/tasks.py
@@ -162,7 +162,14 @@ def get_relation_embeddings(relation_names, model_embed = None):
 
     else: # Assuming jinaai or other models
         model_hf_name = "jinaai/jina-embeddings-v3" # Default for this branch
-        model = AutoModel.from_pretrained(model_hf_name, trust_remote_code=True)
+        # Pin the commit. trust_remote_code=True means transformers executes
+        # custom_st.py out of this repository, and without a revision that is
+        # whatever the repository holds on the day of the run -- so both the
+        # code that runs and the weights it loads could change underneath a
+        # result. The relation graph SEMMA builds from these embeddings is half
+        # its model, so "reproducible" has to cover this too.
+        _rev = os.environ.get("JINA_REVISION") or None
+        model = AutoModel.from_pretrained(model_hf_name, revision=_rev, trust_remote_code=True)
         model.to(device)
         # model.encode for jinaai typically returns numpy arrays
         raw_embeddings = model.encode(relation_names, task="text-matching", truncate_dim=64)
